# SNIP architecture (this repository)

This repo is the first **SNIP domain application** (Network Planning & Optimisation), not the entire Simba Network Intelligence Platform.

Read before changing code:

- `docs/implementation/SNIP-IMPLEMENTATION-CONTEXT.md` (§0 is authoritative for scope)
- `docs/implementation/SNIP-IMPLEMENTATION-STATUS.md`
- `docs/architecture/SNIP-PHASE-2-EVENT-TELEMETRY-INTELLIGENCE-ARCHITECTURE.md`
- `docs/implementation/SNIP-PHASE-2-EVENT-TELEMETRY-INTELLIGENCE-SPECIFICATION.md`

## Authorised now

Phase **2** only: synthetic event/telemetry intelligence on the accepted Phase 1B baseline.

```text
Go simulator → Kafka JSON events → Java consumer → PostgreSQL projection
            → temporal context + deterministic trends
            → existing RAG → local LLM → cited recommendation
```

Preserve Phase 1A/1A.1/1B: lexical + stub CI path; `local-ai` uses Ollama (`nomic-embed-text`, `SimpleVectorStore`, `qwen2.5:7b`). Do not vectorize operational telemetry. Do not put Kafka inside `NetworkContextService`.

Default profile remains lexical + stub with Kafka consumption **off**. Enable Kafka only when `snip.kafka-enabled=true`.

## Do not implement

MCP, Agent Factory, autonomous agents, live OSS/NMS/EMS integrations, live gNB/network writes, Schema Registry, Avro, Protobuf, Flink, Spark, Kafka Streams, dedicated time-series DB, EKS/Kubernetes, Kong, ALB, ALICE, RL, billing, Ionic, AWS lock-in, Phase 3.

## Rules

- Extend Phase 1A/1B abstractions. Do not rewrite the slice.
- Keep recommendations and domain APIs read-only. No apply/execute/write-to-network APIs.
- If retrieval is empty, do not fabricate citations.
- Ordinary CI must not download large models. PostgreSQL via Testcontainers remains required. Kafka Testcontainers is allowed for Phase 2 integration tests.
- Implementation markdown lives under `docs/implementation/`. ADRs under `docs/architecture/adr/`.
- Architecture document has architectural authority. Implementation specification is the authorised execution scope.
